    "angles": "They replaced it with a four-cylinder. C63 used to mean 6.2 litres of\nnaturally aspirated V8; the current car is a 2.0 four with a hybrid system.\nSame badge, half the cylinders.\nThe internals came out of the SLS. Forged pistons and rods from the\nsupercar, dropped into a C-Class, for 510 hp with no turbos anywhere.\nAbout 800 built worldwide. Mercedes planned 650 and raised it when demand\ncame in higher than expected.\nThe rear seat was optional \u2014 you could delete it and save 55 pounds, in a\ncar with a back seat as standard equipment.\nWider track front and rear, flared arches, adjustable coilovers, 390mm\nfront discs and a mechanical limited-slip diff.\n05,000 new. They now trade well above that.",
